                <pb facs="0516" n="506" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg506"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2231/192: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gonzalez</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-09T18:00:00-04:00">September 9, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. Referring to your despatch No. 878 of August 26, you are authorized in case
                    of necessity to agree to the rates which we originally requested on hog lard and
                    wheat flour, namely, 30 and 10 centavos per gross kilo respectively.</p>
                <p>The Department is studying the question of converting specific duties into
                    dollars for the purpose of persuading Ecuador to consent to bind certain rates
                    and will instruct you in this regard in the near future.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
